Mistake 5: Missing the Auxiliary When the Main Verb Has No Helper

If the sentence uses a simple present or past tense verb without an auxiliary (like "He works," "She danced"), you must insert do/does/did in the tag. Students stare at the sentence, see no "is" or "has," and freeze. The rule is: V1 → do/does, V2 → did.

