5 Insider Tips Only Experienced Teachers Know
After teaching question tags to over 5,000 SSC and Bank aspirants, here are the tips that make the biggest difference:

Tip 1: Read the Tag First, Not the Statement

In error detection questions, start by reading the tag. Ask yourself: "Does this tag match the polarity and auxiliary of the statement?" This reverse approach catches 80% of errors in under 10 seconds.

Tip 2: Circle Hidden Negatives in 2 Seconds

Train your eye to spot hardly, scarcely, barely, never, no, none, nobody, nothing, neither, nor instantly. When you see one, the tag MUST be positive. No exceptions.

Tip 3: "Used to" Always Takes "Didn't" in the Tag

This is a favorite examiner trap. "He used to smoke" → "didn't he?" Not "usedn't he?" The "used to" form in modern English takes "did" as the auxiliary in tags.

Tip 4: "Need" and "Dare" as Modals Take No "S"

When "need" or "dare" are used as modal verbs (without "to"), the tag uses them directly: "He need not go, need he?" This appears in 1 out of every 3 Bank PO papers.

Tip 5: Compound Subjects with "Not Only...But Also" Follow the Second Subject

"Not only Ram but also Shyam is coming" → the tag matches "Shyam" (the second subject): "isn't he?" This is an advanced trap that appears in SSC CGL Mains.

